# Agent git workflow

Never edit on `main`. At the start of a task, create a dedicated branch and worktree, then do all remaining work there.

```bash
git fetch origin
git worktree add -b agent/<short-task-slug> ../commander-decks-<short-task-slug> origin/main
```

Reuse that worktree for the rest of the session. Do not share a branch or worktree with another agent. If already inside a unique `agent/*` worktree for this task, keep using it.

## Commits

Commit without waiting for the user to ask. After each coherent step (for example: save decklist, resolve cards, primer + README link), create a commit with a 1–2 sentence message focused on why.

- Do not amend published commits
- Do not commit secrets or unrelated shared-cache noise

## Finish

When the task is done:

1. Inspect the full diff; drop unrelated cache or registry files
2. `git push -u origin HEAD`
3. Open a ready-for-review PR (`draft: false`) summarizing what changed
4. Follow [Hosted CI before completion](../../AGENTS.md#hosted-ci-before-completion):
   run `gh pr checks <pr-number> --watch` (or explicitly poll) for every check on
   the latest head and current PR metadata, including **PR title**. Confirm both
   **CI** and **PR title** have reported checks. Repeat after every push or
   metadata edit and verify correction reruns. **GitHub Pages** runs on `main` or
   manual dispatch and is not expected on PR branches; inspect it if reported.
5. Fix introduced failures; follow [the defect reporting rule](../../.github/ISSUES.md)
   for uncertain or reproduced baseline failures. Never assume they are pre-existing.
6. Return the PR URL with separate local-validation and hosted-CI results. Wait
   for every reported check before claiming CI passed or full validation; link
   each unresolved pending, blocked, or failing check.

Title the PR as `<area>: <imperative summary>` from [`.github/PULL_REQUESTS.md`](../../../.github/PULL_REQUESTS.md). Numbered Rule DSL work is `dsl: Part N …`. The **PR title** workflow rejects other shapes.

Create the PR with `gh pr create --base main --head <branch>` and confirm it is not a draft. If `gh` is missing or unauthenticated, say so and return `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/compare/main...<branch>?expand=1` instead.

If `gh` cannot inspect checks, poll the GitHub PR checks page with another tool
or browser. Without authenticated access, report hosted CI as blocked and link
the checks page (or compare URL if no PR exists); missing access is not a pass.

## Deck modification PRs

When a PR changes an existing `decks/<deck>/decklist.txt`, the body must include a Cards in / Cards out table with every card linked to Scryfall. Generate it rather than writing it by hand:

```bash
python3 .agents/skills/deck-workspace/scripts/deck_change_table.py decks/<deck> --base origin/main
```

Place the result under a `## Cards in / Cards out` heading. The script sorts each column alphabetically and zips them, so its rows are not real swaps: re-pair them into the swaps actually intended and add a `Reason` column giving the reason for each one. Check the final table against the script output so no card is dropped. When one change lands in several stages, use one table per stage rather than forcing unrelated cards into the same row. A deck PR that only adds a new deck does not need the table.
